  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Look at my garden grow! Kitchen gardening by young women and men with disabilities to improve family food security and income even during crises.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through their own sustainable kitchen gardens, 176 young persons with disabilities (106F 70M aged 17-30) in 2 districts in Uganda have improved food security, income and dietary diversity (plus that of their 704 household members), also reducing their experience of violence. Young people with disabilities&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; own local organisations have the peer trainers, learning sites, organisational strength and links to government needed to sustain and grow the approach.</narrative>
  </description>
